{"name":"Macaroni","hex":"#f3d085","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"macaroni","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of pasta in the form of short tubes, typically boiled and served in soup, with a sauce, or in melted cheese; a dish of this. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Pasta, particularly thicker noodles, spaghetti."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Chic, fashionable, stylish; in the manner of a macaroni."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/macaroni"}],"entries":[{"title":"Macaroni","blocks":[{"text":"Macaroni, known in Italian as maccheroni, is a pasta shaped like narrow tubes. Made with durum wheat, macaroni is commonly cut in short lengths; curved macaroni may be referred to as \"elbow macaroni\". Some home machines can make macaroni shapes but, like most pasta, macaroni is usually made commercially by large-scale extrusion. The common curved shape is created by different speeds of extrusion on opposite sides of the pasta tube as it comes out of the machine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Macaroni2.jpg/330px-Macaroni2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macaroni","wikidata":"Q20019"},{"title":"Macaroni (fashion)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Macaroni\" was a pejorative term used to describe a fashionable fellow of 18th-century Britain. Stereotypically, men in the macaroni subculture dressed, spoke, and behaved in an androgynous manner. The term \"macaroni\" pejoratively referred to a man who \"exceeded the ordinary bounds of fashion\" in terms of high-end clothing, fastidious eating, and gambling. He mixed Continental affectations with his British nature, like a practitioner of macaronic verse, laying himself open to satire."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Richard_Cosway_by_Richard_Cosway.jpg/330px-Richard_Cosway_by_Richard_Cosway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macaroni_(fashion)","wikidata":"Q1882537"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Elbow_macaroni_die_front.jpg/250px-Elbow_macaroni_die_front.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Elbow_macaroni_die_front.jpg/250px-Elbow_macaroni_die_front.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AElbow_macaroni_die_front.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Elbow_macaroni_die_back.jpg/250px-Elbow_macaroni_die_back.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Elbow_macaroni_die_back.jpg/250px-Elbow_macaroni_die_back.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AElbow_macaroni_die_back.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Philip_Dawe%2C_The_Macaroni._A_Real_Character_at_the_Late_Masquerade_%281773%29.jpg/500px-Philip_Dawe%2C_The_Macaroni._A_Real_Character_at_the_Late_Masquerade_%281773%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Philip_Dawe%2C_The_Macaroni._A_Real_Character_at_the_Late_Masquerade_%281773%29.jpg/500px-Philip_Dawe%2C_The_Macaroni._A_Real_Character_at_the_Late_Masquerade_%281773%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"The Macaroni. A real Character at the late Masquerade\", mezzotint by Philip Dawe, 1773","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhilip_Dawe%2C_The_Macaroni._A_Real_Character_at_the_Late_Masquerade_(1773).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wiki